Z||000012||rogergarrison||10-25-2001||07:10 PM||||I used 1/8" aluminum to make the inner bucket to mount Hella Driving lite (for low) and Blue Ion (for high). The plate is bolted onto the same studs as the orig Fiero assembly. Its then covered with 3/16" lexan with the edges painted as a surround to match the car. They also stay put when the hood is opened, so required some cutting and fiberglass work.<p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 10-25-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000013||Pontiaddict||10-25-2001||08:59 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by TRiAD:<BR><B> Purple Pavement Eater? <BR>If so, it was actually a fastback originally, but was converted to be different from Big Blue. <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Nope not the PPE either. <A HREF="http://www.v8archie.com/johnson.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.v8archie.com/johnson.htm</A> <BR>It's an actual chopped notchback.<BR>Very cool car too.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000014||artherd||10-26-2001||01:28 AM||||I've just got these now:<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/hid/hid1.jpg"> <P>I am working on adapting dual-round (think BMW's 'angel eyes') projection lenses, while still keeping the flip-up design.   They will only 'flip up' about half as far though, lowered headlights!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Best!<BR>Ben<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000015||grinthock||10-26-2001||12:23 PM||||Slammed did a round conversion -- looks good.||||reg||1
Z||000016||VISCERAL||10-26-2001||01:55 PM||||Hey atherd, i read somewhere you are using hid headlamps from a doner car. Which one? What does one have to do to replace the stock lights for hid's||||reg||1
Z||000017||artherd||10-28-2001||02:16 AM||||Pretty easy, you juse need a set of H4 lamp housings (West Coast Fieros and FieroStore sell them)<P>Then you buy a set of HID lamps with H4 socketed bulbs, find somewhere to mount the ballasts, and that's it!<P>I did buy my HID lamps new, not from a donor car (used 23KV transformers at *exceptionally* leathal currents scare me...)<P>Love the light output, it's just amazing.  No comparison to filament lights, it just has to be seen to be belived.  <P>I have people frequently ride up alongside me on the freeway at night...   seems they can see better next to my car..<P>Total cost: about $~700.  Worth it so many times over.<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P><BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by VISCERAL:<BR><B>Hey atherd, i read somewhere you are using hid headlamps from a doner car. Which one? What does one have to do to replace the stock lights for hid's</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000018||SLYGUY||10-28-2001||02:28 AM||||I'm sorry artherd but it looks like the passenger side headlight it about 4-5 inches closer to the windshield than the driver's side headlight. I've seen that pic before and I think that I'm the only one that sees it. <BR>I don't see any illumination difference either. <BR>Glad it worked out well for you, but can you explain the optical illusion to me?<P>Does anybody else see this?<P>Sly||||reg||1
Z||000019||artherd||10-28-2001||06:36 PM||||It's a crappy picture  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  (distortion is caused by the wide lense I used, creates increased paralax, shrinks things far away more then they naturally appear to be...)<P>I'll have to take a pick with a normal Fiero's lights in the same frame.  It's pretty dramatic.<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P><BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by SLYGUY:<BR><B>I'm sorry artherd but it looks like the passenger side headlight it about 4-5 inches closer to the windshield than the driver's side headlight. I've seen that pic before and I think that I'm the only one that sees it. <BR>I don't see any illumination difference either. <BR>Glad it worked out well for you, but can you explain the optical illusion to me?<P>Does anybody else see this?<P>Sly</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||1
